# The login-screen brand is part of the product identity, not a preference.
# (Wallpaper is deliberately NOT locked — users may change their own.)
/org/gnome/login-screen/logo
# Shell extensions come with the image; none are fetched from the internet.
# The set an account has ENABLED is not locked: kosher-layout writes it per
# account at sign-in (see 20-kosheros-desktop), and dconf locks are global.
/org/gnome/shell/allow-extension-installation
# No donation appeals on a family computer (see 20-kosheros-desktop).
/org/gnome/settings-daemon/plugins/housekeeping/donation-reminder-enabled
